			<staticText>
				<reportElement uuid="e73e89d1-88fa-4341-b453-1d13bb9558f7" x="0" y="60" width="572" height="131"/>
				<textElement>
					<font fontName="DejaVu Sans" size="8"/>
				</textElement>
				<text><![CDATA[Notes
*       This report includes licences with an AAC in timber supply areas, tree farm licences, and pulpwood agreements derived
         from apportioned volume.
*       Licences are linked to a corporate group or company if the corporate group or company is affiliated with or controls the
         licence holder, as defined by Section 53 of the Forest Act.
*       A corporate group or company is displayed if they hold 2 or more licences, or if it holds a licence with an AAC greater than
         or equal to 100,000 m3.
*       INDEPENDENT MEDIUM licences have an AAC greater than or equal to 25,000 m3 and less than 100,000 m3.
*       INDEPENDENT SMALL licences have an AAC less than 25,000 m3.
*       JOINTLY HELD LICENCES are licences held by more than one corporate group or company.
*       PROVINCIAL AAC Total is the Sum of the TFL and TSA AAC's; excludes issued Woodlot Licences, Community Forest Agreements and 
         First Nation Woodland Licences.
]]></text>
			</staticText>
